sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-anthrobots-10> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-10--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-10--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on levin-2024-anthrobots-10: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.35" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.349"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "needs-new-data" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.75"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "A transition matrix among movement labels is a standard calculation and would rank persistence if the segment labels were public. They are not. The result also depends on the unpublished clustering step, so neither the rank order nor the intermediate status of eclectic motion can be recomputed now." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: From labeled 30-second segments, estimate the Markov transition matrix among circular, linear, curvilinear and eclectic states over the five-hour recordings. Circular self-transition highest, and eclectic outflow into the other three states, would support the stability order; a high eclectic self-transition, or frequent circular-to-linear switches, would refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Segment labels and the transition counts are not deposited.", "The eclectic class is defined as whatever is left over, so its role as an intermediate is partly by construction.", "Stability ranks inherit whatever cluster boundaries were chosen upstream." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2024-anthrobots-10--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of levin-2024-anthrobots-10 by Grok 4.7: 0.86" ;
